This study is part of the ECAPOV (ECA databank project) - a major initiative for harmonization of households' surveys in Eastern Europe and Central Asia (ECA). The ECAPOV archive contains harmonized microdata from 27 low - and middle-income countries in ECA region for the 1999-2010 period. A unique standardization methodology has been developed and implemented for construction of harmonized consumption aggregates as well as standardized modules including demographic roster, labor, education, income, and social protection.
