abstract:
The main purpose of the survey is to collect information providing a detailed description of living standards as well as an essential database to help define and evaluate social programs allowing a higher level of living. better social integration of low-income households in the development process. These include:

- provide a database on the population's access to basic social services (literacy, education, health, housing, etc.);
- to identify and analyze the characteristics of the most vulnerable social groups and towards which the social assistance of the State must be directed;
- to study the socio-economic environment of households by examining the use of community and social services made available to the population and the effects on their well-being;
- to produce and update a series of socio-economic indicators, both quantitative and qualitative, allowing the various bodies and ministerial departments to take decisions based on data safe;
- grasp the extent of the inequalities between the different social groups and the various regions of the country;
- obtain integrated data on a large number of variables in order to highlight the links existing between the various demographic and socio-economic determinants of the standard of living.

cleaning_operations:
MNAPOV is a new data collection effort enacted in 2014 and managed by MNATSD. It covers 36 surveys from 11 countries. Two data points (surveys) are available for each country, except Algeria. 
The database is organized in 3 modules following the Global Monitoring Database (GMD) Harmonization guidelines, including the welfare aggregate which is used for Global Poverty Monitoring. 
Terms of use of the data adhere to agreements with the original data producers.

A data entry program has been developed to enter the survey data. This includes a control program which performs an automatic verification as the information is recorded. In addition, the clearance phase of the survey files required the development of a special data consistency control program which revolves around the points following:

- Identifier control (geographic code);
- Exhaustiveness check of the PUs surveyed;
- Coupling of the different files;
- Presence control of compulsory cards;
- Attendance control of household members;
- Control by return to basic documents;
- Control of the expenditure questionnaire;
- Automatic correction phase.

These different control programs are started one at a time by menu or functionally grouped into specified procedures. Due to the interactive correction that they must undergo, the data files are all converted from the start of this phase in the workstation where the adjustments planned at the level are made. of the organization of the decided proceedings.

abstract:
The main purpose of the survey is to collect information providing a detailed description of living standards as well as an essential database to help define and evaluate social programs allowing a higher level of living, better social integration of low-income households in the development process. These include in particular:

- analyze the level and trends of household spending according to the different consumption functions and the main socio-economic characteristics of heads of households;
- analyze the levels, sources and inequalities in terms of income;
- update poverty indicators;
- study aspects related to distribution and inequalities in the standard of living;
- provide the basic data necessary for the development of programs in the field of economic and social planning and for decision-making;
- assess the impact of economic and social measures on the living conditions of households, in particular with regard to changes in structure and consumption expenditure;
- analyze certain aspects of the living conditions of the population (housing, durable goods equipment, transfers, sources of income, etc.);
- provide the data necessary for research in the socio-economic field.

cleaning_operations:
MNAPOV is a new data collection effort enacted in 2014 and managed by MNATSD. It covers 36 surveys from 11 countries. Two data points (surveys) are available for each country, except Algeria. 
The database is organized in 3 modules following the Global Monitoring Database (GMD) Harmonization guidelines, including the welfare aggregate which is used for Global Poverty Monitoring. 
Terms of use of the data adhere to agreements with the original data producers.

A data entry program has been developed to enter the survey data. This includes a control program which performs an automatic verification as the information is recorded. In addition, the data consistency check was carried out in four main stages:

- The first step consists of:
+ check the validity of the identifiers and geographic codes for the 4 questionnaires taken in isolation;
+ check the presence of questionnaires 2 and 3 using the data from questionnaire 1;
+ check the presence of questionnaire 4 for rural primary units;
+ check the concordance of the identifiers of the questionnaires (1, 2 and 3) possibly filled in for the same household;
+ list the number of households entered (questionnaire 1) and the number of women observed, i.e. the number of type 2 and 3 questionnaires.

- The second step: It can only be started once the inconsistencies of the first step have been corrected. Its purpose is to ensure the presence of compulsory cards at the level of the four questionnaires of the survey.

- The third step: Consists of a series of compulsory checks of the basic variables (sex, age, ...). It can only be addressed once the inconsistencies revealed by the second step are rectified.

- The last step: Also depends on the completion of the previous steps. Contrary to the first three stages which require a systematic return to the collection documents, this stage is characterized by a possible automatic correction process of the decided inconsistencies. Depending on the scope and frequency of errors detected.

Les contrôleurs, aidés par les enquêteurs, ont effectué les premiers contrôles sur terrain et les superviseurs vérifiaient systématiquement les données et les cohérences des informations reçues (sauts, population de référence, modalité déterminante, ...). Le contrôle de vraisemblance des réponses au niveau des montants relatifs aux revenus et dépenses, accapare la majorité des temps de contrôle et nécessite un traitement informatique spécial pour être mises à jour directement après consultation des questionnaires.

La saisie des données a été centralisée à la Direction des Statistiques des Ménages, assurée par 9 agents de saisie et 3 vérificateurs de saisie pendant une durée de 3 mois et 3 mois pour les vérifications et corrections. Le logiciel de saisie utilisé est l’IMPS (Integrated Microcomputer Processing System) version 3.1.

Au niveau du traitement informatique, les types de contrôle suivants ont été effectués:
- Contrôle des identifiants, des omissions et des doublons;
- Contrôles des variables à l’intérieur d’un enregistrement;
- Contrôle des données à l’intérieur d’une section;
- Contrôle des renseignements entre deux sections différentes;
- Contrôles des vraisemblances des variables quantitatives sur les revenus et dépenses;
- Contrôle des écarts;
- Contrôle de la production agricole.

abstract:
l'Objectif de l'enquête est de fournir au gouvernement et aux autorités malgache, de façon périodique, des données récentes multi-thèmes sur les conditions de vie des ménages malgache, permettant essentiellement de :
- suivre l’évolution du niveau de vie des Malagasy;
- suivre l’évolution des indicateurs sociaux (santé, éducation et emploi);
- actualiser la Matrice de Comptabilité Sociale de Madagascar;
- suivre l’évolution de la situation nutritionnelle;
- mettre à jour le panier de la ménagère;
- prendre en compte les aspects sociaux dans la formulation des politiques économiques.

Les groupes cibles de l’analyse sont les salariés (publics et privés) et les indépendants en milieu urbain, les cultivateurs, les éleveurs et les Pêcheurs en milieu rural.

